<li>Update the remarks on the Jacobian conjecture and add a footnote
with the counterexample.
<li>In the proof of Severi (3.2.9), change the main computation
to come from the chain rule rather than applying the CR vector field
to \(F.\)  Hopefully this makes the computation a little clearer
(and it emphasizes where the CR vector field comes from).
<li>In the proof of Theorem 4.5.3, emphasize that \(\chi\) is smooth
and be more precise in the language.
<li>Add "proper subvariety" to the index.
<li>In Example 6.5.2, add the possibility of using the zero function to
define the entire euclidean space as a subvariety.

See https://www.jirka.org/scv/changes.html for older changes.
